    "error_map": {
        "400": "invalid_request",
        "401": "auth_expired",
        "403": "permission_denied",
        "404": "invalid_request",
        "405": "invalid_request",
        "425": "provider_transient",
        "500": "provider_transient",
        "502": "provider_transient",
        "503": "provider_transient",
        "504": "provider_transient"
    },
    "_error_map_note": "Story 26.5 decision (closes the dossier's open point for core/pull_errors.py): Amazon reporting errors carry NO stable numeric provider sub-codes (body = {code, details} with free-text details), so the map keys are HTTP-STATUS-ONLY and the CONNECTOR applies them itself (module-side status lookup with classify_http_error as fallback) -- core's '<status>:<provider_code>' contract is untouched (no wildcard added to core). Module-level refinements on details substrings: 'KDP authors do not have access to Sponsored Brands functionality' -> permission_denied; 'Not authorized to access scope' -> permission_denied; 'Tactic T00020 is not supported for report API in marketplace' -> invalid_request; 'Report date is too far in the past' -> invalid_request (retention floor, also refused pre-call). Poll-time 401s are a documented transient quirk: retried x5 before classifying auth_expired. 425 (duplicate report) is NOT an error: the socle claim/request-hash dedup reuses the in-flight reportId (a residual provider 425 re-reads the persisted ref, never blind-resubmits). Report status FAILED maps to the canonical 'expired' poll status when the failureReason is not configuration (single socle resubmission, then provider_transient); configuration failureReasons raise invalid_request. 429 + Retry-After stays on the core.quota.RateLimitError breaker path, never in this map.",
    "refetch": {
        "nightly_days": 3,
        "weekly_days": 14,
        "monthly_days": 45,
        "_note": "Dossier section 1.7: traffic is corrected up to 3 days after the click date (nightly 3); conversions are restated 1/7/28 days after the conversion event and are reported on the AD-INTERACTION date, so with 14-day attribution a value can move up to 42 days (weekly 14 / monthly 45 covers the tail inside the SB 60-day retention floor). AD-7 supersede-by-pull_id makes every re-pull idempotent."
    },
